title: Proposition 18
---
order: 18
---
short_label: XI.18
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a straight line is at right angles to any plane, then all the planes through it are also at right angles to the same plane.
----
proof:

Let any straight line {AB} be at right angles to the plane of reference.

I say that all the planes through {AB} are also at right angles to the plane of reference.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="290" height="220" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.18 diagram" src="propXI18.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the plane of reference P in oblique view, AB at right
    // angles to it, the plane DE through AB cutting it in CE, and FG drawn
    // in DE at right angles to CE.
    //
    // Added, all transparent: PT and DET, faceless twins of the filled
    // planes P and DE (raised over the figure if highlighted, #140); CE,
    // the intersection, which Joyce's figure draws only as the plane's
    // edge; and the right-angle squares at B (ABF, by XI.Def.3) and at F
    // (GFB, by construction).
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): X, Y, Z, P0, P2, A free;
    // B, E, F sliders. E arrives with the plane DE and F is "taken at
    // random on CE", so both are deferred. P1, P3, C, D, G are derived
    // and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["P","PT","P1","P3","A","B","AB"];
    var PLANE = GIVEN.concat(["C","D","E","DE","DET"]);
    var SEC   = PLANE.concat(["CE"]);
    var FGv   = SEC.concat(["F","G","FG","angGFB"]);
    var ALL   = FGv.concat(["angABF"]);
