            "P0;point;free;30,200;0;0,75,100",
            "P2;point;free;260,70;0;0,75,100",
            "P1;point;intersection;P0,X,P2,Z;0;0",
            "P3;point;intersection;P2,X,P0,Z;0;0",
            "P;polygon;quadrilateral;P0,P1,P2,P3;0;0;lightGray;brighter",
            "A;point;free;180,40",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A,Y,180,140",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "E;point;lineSlider;P1,P2,200,120",
            "C;point;intersection;E,B,P0,P3",
            "D;point;parallelogram;A,B,C",
            "DE;polygon;parallelogram;D,C,E;0;0;black;random",
            "F;point;lineSlider;C,E,100,150",
            "G;point;intersection;A,D,F,Y",
            "FG;line;connect;F,G",
            // Transparent highlight targets.
            "PT;polygon;quadrilateral;P0,P1,P2,P3;0;0;0;0",
            "DET;polygon;parallelogram;D,C,E;0;0;0;0",
            "CE;line;connect;C,E;0;0;0",
            "angABF;sector;angleMarkerRight;B,A,F",
            "angGFB;sector;angleMarkerRight;F,G,B"
        ],
        deferDraggables: ["E","F"],
        aliases: { "ABF": "angABF", "FBA": "angABF",
                   "GFB": "angGFB", "BFG": "angGFB" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“If a straight line is at right angles to any plane,”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XI.18" }] },
            { text: "“then all the planes through it are also at right angles to the same plane.”",
              visible: PLANE,
              highlighted: ["AB","DET","PT"] },
            { text: "Let any straight line {AB} be at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"] },
            { text: "I say that all the planes through {AB} are also at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"] },
            { text: "Let the plane {DE|DET} be drawn through {AB}.",
              visible: PLANE,
              highlighted: ["DET","AB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "DE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Let {CE} be the intersection of the plane {DE|DET} and the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: SEC,
              highlighted: ["CE","DET","PT"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "CE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Take a point {F} at random on {CE},",
              visible: SEC.concat(["F"]),
              highlighted: ["F","CE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "F", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and draw {FG} from {F} at right angles to {CE} in the plane {DE|DET}.",
              visible: FGv,
              highlighted: ["FG","CE","angGFB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "FG",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "G",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "angGFB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "FG at right angles to CE", ref: "I.11" }] },
            { text: "Now, since {AB} is at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT},",
              visible: FGv,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"] },
            { text: "therefore {AB} is also at right angles to all the straight lines which meet it and lie in the {plane of reference|PT},",
              visible: FGv,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "a line at right angles to a plane", ref: "XI.Def.3" }] },
            { text: "so that it is also at right angles to {CE}. Therefore the angle {ABF|angABF} is right.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CE","angABF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angABF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "But the angle {GFB|angGFB} is also right, therefore {AB} is parallel to {FG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["angGFB","angABF","AB","FG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB parallel to FG", ref: "I.28" }] },
            { text: "But {AB} is at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"] },
            { text: "therefore {FG} is also at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","PT"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "parallel to a line at right angles to a plane", ref: "XI.8" }] },
            { text: "Now a plane is at right angles to a plane when the straight lines drawn in one of the planes",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DET","PT"] },
            { text: "at right angles to the intersection of the planes are at right angles to the remaining plane.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CE","FG","PT"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "planes at right angles", ref: "XI.Def.4" }] },
            { text: "And {FG}, drawn in one of the planes {DE|DET} at right angles to {CE}, the intersection of the planes,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","DET","CE","angGFB"] },
            { text: "was proved to be at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","PT"] },
            { text: "Therefore the plane {DE|DET} is at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DET","PT"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DE at right angles to the plane", ref: "XI.Def.4" }] },
            { text: "Similarly it can also be proved that all the planes through {AB} are at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"] },
            { text: "Therefore, if a straight line is at right angles to any plane,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"] },
            { text: "then all the planes through it are also at right angles to the same plane.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","DET","PT"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.18") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.11":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI11/",
        "I.28":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI28/",
        "XI.Def.3": "/elements/books/bookXI/definitions/defXI3/",
        "XI.Def.4": "/elements/books/bookXI/definitions/defXI4/",
        "XI.8":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI8/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Let the plane {DE|DET} be drawn through {AB}. Let {CE} be the intersection of the plane {DE|DET} and the plane of reference.

Take a point {F} at random on {CE}, and draw {FG} from {F} at right angles to {CE} in the plane {DE|DET}. [!just I.11]

Now, since {AB} is at right angles to the plane of reference, therefore {AB} is also at right angles to all the straight lines which meet it and lie in the plane of reference, so that it is also at right angles to {CE}. Therefore the angle {ABF} is right. [!just XI.Def.3]

But the angle {GFB} is also right, therefore {AB} is parallel to {FG}. [!just I.28]

But {AB} is at right angles to the plane of reference, therefore {FG} is also at right angles to the plane of reference. [!just XI.8]

Now a plane is at right angles to a plane when the straight lines drawn in one of the planes at right angles to the intersection of the planes are at right angles to the remaining plane. And {FG}, drawn in one of the planes {DE|DET} at right angles to {CE}, the intersection of the planes, was proved to be at right angles to the plane of reference. Therefore the plane {DE|DET} is at right angles to the plane of reference. [!just XI.Def.4]

Similarly it can also be proved that all the planes through {AB} are at right angles to the plane of reference.

Therefore, *if a straight line is at right angles to any plane, then all the planes through it are also at right angles to the same plane.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
